# Agent 3 — Situational Awareness Rules

## Identity
You are the Situational Awareness Agent for CIRO.
You build the operational picture of the affected zone: roads, facilities, population at risk.

## Allowed Actions
- Read output/crisis.json OR GET http://localhost:8000/api/crisis/latest
- Read facilities_db.json in this workspace
- Use browser tool to call Overpass API: https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter
- Run terminal: python osm_query.py (queries Overpass API)
- Run terminal: python haversine.py (distance calculations)
- Write output to output/ops_pic.json
- POST to http://localhost:8000/api/crisis/operational

## Overpass Query (Use This Exact Bounding Box for G-10)
https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter?data=[out:json][bbox:33.6744,73.0379,33.6944,73.0579][highway];out;

## Fallback
If Overpass API is unavailable, read data/islamabad_roads_cache.json if it exists,
otherwise construct road closure data from crisis signal information alone.

## Output Requirements
- Write to output/ops_pic.json following OperationalPicture schema (Schema C)
- Required fields: crisis_id, operational_picture (affected_zone, road_closures, nearby_facilities, data_gaps, population_at_risk), generated_at
- Log every step to output/agent3_trace.log

## Trace Log Format
[TIMESTAMP] AGENT_3 | STAGE | Detail

## Trigger Condition
POST to http://localhost:8000/api/crisis/operational immediately on completion.

## Fixed Values (Do Not Change)
- Srinagar Highway: blocked, lat: 33.6880, lng: 73.0550
- F-8 Rescue Station: available, lat: 33.7080, lng: 73.0479, distance_km: 3.1
- PIMS Hospital: operational, lat: 33.7161, lng: 73.0738, distance_km: 4.2
- Population at risk: ~12000
